> Of course, Elbereth helps ;)

When I first enter the mines I like to cast a spell of force bolt,
kill one gnome, pick up the body, go back up the stairs, eat
it, make sure I am at full hit points and at least some manna
points.  Then lather rinse repeat until there is no crowd and I
am Satiated.  If there's time to explore any levels in the main
dungeon in the process that's good.

I can end up doing a level in the mines, a level in Sokoban,
in alternation before I get to minetown doing it this way.
Stack items near the down stairs as I progress through each
level.  I Sokoban to move them down into the main dungeon,
in the mines to move them down towards the minetown altar.

It's a lot of running away and moving among levels.  That
gives plenty of time to encounter randomly generated monsters
instead of crowds.

Doing this exercises attack spells so enhance them as you
level up.  Doing the same with daggers also enhances them.
Exactly what order I enhance between spells and daggers
isn't constitant but daggers tend to go first because until
intelligence gets high enough spells cost food and daggers
don't.



